From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:20:08 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: lower an AND with a complemented operand to BIC

`a & !b` and `!b & a` on registers of the operation's size were rejected
at assembly generation ("invalid rexpr for oprd"), although BIC computes
exactly a AND NOT b. They are now lowered to BIC, with the complemented
operand second; a shift or rotation of that operand is folded into BIC's
shifted-register form, as for AND.

The lowering proof covers both operand orders. The tests cover both
orders, a shifted operand, a complemented constant (folded beforehand
into an AND with an immediate) and two complemented operands, which
remain rejected.
---
